I'm a software engineer, homelabber, and occasional blogger. I like over-engineering things, and bring up Nix far more than is necessary.

I grew up in Hong Kong, and have studied for a bit in the USA and UK. I currently live/work in London.

Beyond my desk, I enjoy the gym, cooking, and gaming. Unfortunately, I'm hardstuck Bronze in League of Legends and Silver in Overwatch.

In my spare time, I like working on my projects, which mainly pertain to my own tools and devkit. I love that our field is as vast as it is, and prefer reading textbooks to keep up with everything I've learnt in the past, but also to learn new things and make me a better engineer.

I'm particularly interested in the intersection of compilers, programming languages, and AI.

[Say hi](mailto:ujaandas03@gmail.com) - I like talking to people who build things too.
